VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED
REASON: This PR is not superseded. None of the detector PRs (#15–#20) touch the hosted demo, welcome tab or config work. But it still targets `backend-rest`, and `hosted/` imports `backend/src/agent.js`, so it can't be judged as mergeable against current main until it is retargeted and rebased. There is also a real behaviour bug in the hosted `/api/classify` stub.

- **Wrong base.** `mergeable=CLEAN` is against `backend-rest`, not main. Retarget to main and rebase on `6ca2a34`, then confirm two things on main: that `backend/src/agent.js` exports `protectDeal`, and that the README section about the REST adapter (step 4/5, `PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET is required…`) actually exists there. If #1 hasn't merged, this PR either carries #1's changes or ships a broken Worker import.
- **AI check breaks results on the hosted server.** `/api/classify` returns `503 llm_off`, but `/health` says `llm: "off"`. If a tester ticks "Ask the backend for an AI check", every call goes down the LLM-error path. Per SPEC that caps verdicts at medium with `llm:"error"`, so the bike thread stops showing **High risk**. Either have `background.js` skip classify when health reports `llm:"off"`, or disable or hide the checkbox when the hosted backend is selected.
- **Diff is cut off.** It ends at `hosted/static/favicon.svg`. I can't see `wrangler.toml` (it needs a Durable Object binding `ORDERS` plus a `new_sqlite_classes: ["MockOrders"]` migration), the `package.json` scripts (`hosted:deploy`, `pack:extension`, `e2e:hosted`) or the hosted e2e. Please post the rest before approval.
- **`MAX_ORDERS` isn't a per-day cap.** `alarm()` sets `meta:count` to the number of surviving orders, and only re-arms if some remain. So the cap really limits live orders over a rolling window. Fix the comment or the logic, and check that the "Try again tomorrow" message is still true.
- **LAN regression in `demo/checkout-return.html`.** A plain-http, non-localhost host (e.g. `http://192.168.1.5:8080`, used for phone testing) used to reach `hostname:8787` and now falls back to `localhost:8787`. Keep the old `hostname:8787` branch for any `http:` host.
- **Check the storage keys.** `welcome.js` reads `pb_opts.backendUrl`. Make sure that matches exactly what `options.js` and `background.js` write, or the demo button will always point at the hosted URL.
- **Fixed delay on the "not running" hint.** On a slow first load, the 2.5 s timeout can show the yellow box even when the extension is installed. Remove the note if `dataset.paybrake` flips to `"on"` later (a MutationObserver on `<html>` would do it).
- **Minor.** The hosted worker's CORS check accepts any `chrome-extension://` origin. That's fine for a mock server, but note it in TESTING.md as intentional. Also, the copy rename "Switch to a PayPal order" is applied consistently, so re-run `tests/copy.test.mjs` and the e2e selectors after the rebase.
